+    ``H_out`` present it is TurboBoA's Kronecker row/column quadratic:
+
+    ``tr(H_out @ dW @ H_in @ dW.T)``
+
+    plus the existing ``dXXT`` residual term.  The derivation assumes the
+    damped Hessians are symmetric, matching the solver's Cholesky contract.
+    Degenerate zero-code coordinates have a zero denominator and are left
+    unchanged instead of producing NaNs.
